# OtterWorks Trivy Ignore List
#
# Every entry follows the format documented in docs/labs/security-sprint-guide.md:
#   # CVE — <package>: <description>
#   # Impact: <sev>. Tracked in <ticket>. Blocked on <reason>. Revisit by <date>.
#   CVE-ID
#
# Rules:
# - Exact IDs only. Trivy's plain-text ignore file does not expand globs, so a
#   pattern such as `CVE-2021-*` suppresses nothing and only hides the intent.
# - One block per module. A suppression is removed as soon as the fixed version
#   is a patch/minor bump; only major-version-gated fixes stay here.
# - report-service is excluded via `scan.skip-dirs` in
#   security/scanning/trivy-config.yaml (intentional legacy Java 8 service kept
#   for the dependency-cve-remediation exercise), so it has no entries here.
# - Ticket IDs use the OTTERWORKS-SEC-<n> placeholder until a tracker exists.

# ============================================================================
# frontend/admin-dashboard — Angular 17.3.12 (fixed in 19.2.x / 20.3.x / 21.x)
# All fixes require the Angular 17 -> 19+ major upgrade (two majors, new
# application builder, signal-based APIs). The dashboard is an internal
# operator UI served behind the shared ingress with no SSR/hydration and no
# HttpTransferCache, so the SSR/cache issues are not reachable as deployed.
# ============================================================================

# CVE-2025-66035 — @angular/common: HttpClient XSRF token leakage via protocol-relative URLs
# Impact: HIGH. Tracked in OTTERWORKS-SEC-101. Blocked on Angular 19+ major upgrade. Revisit by 2026-12-31.
CVE-2025-66035
