# ============================================================================
# services/collab-service — @opentelemetry/sdk-node 0.49.1 (fixed in 0.217.0+)
# The OpenTelemetry JS SDK is pre-1.0; 0.49 -> 0.2xx is a breaking upgrade
# (sdk-node/exporter/instrumentation packages must move together, resources
# and semantic-conventions APIs changed). The vulnerable code paths are the
# Jaeger propagator header decoder and the Prometheus exporter, neither of
# which is enabled — collab-service exports over OTLP/HTTP only.
# ============================================================================

# CVE-2026-59892 — @opentelemetry/propagator-jaeger: DoS via malformed HTTP header decoding
# Impact: HIGH. Tracked in OTTERWORKS-SEC-102. Blocked on OpenTelemetry JS SDK 0.49 -> 0.2xx breaking upgrade. Revisit by 2026-12-31.
CVE-2026-59892
# CVE-2026-44902 — @opentelemetry/sdk-node (exporter-prometheus): DoS via malformed HTTP request
# Impact: HIGH. Tracked in OTTERWORKS-SEC-102. Blocked on OpenTelemetry JS SDK 0.49 -> 0.2xx breaking upgrade. Revisit by 2026-12-31.
CVE-2026-44902

